WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:05.730
Actors can try for years to land a decent
role, and even when they do, it's no guarantee

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:06.779
of success.

00:00:06.779 --> 00:00:11.200
Those who manage to make it big often say
the same thing: they were in the right place

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:12.570
at the right time.

00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:16.390
Have a look at the auditions that changed
everything for these actors.

00:00:16.390 --> 00:00:17.390
Daisy Ridley

00:00:17.390 --> 00:00:22.520
Playing Rey in Star Wars: The Force Awakens
catapulted Daisy Ridley onto the A-list.

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:26.800
Hundreds of young actresses auditioned for
the part, including established stars like

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:31.590
Chloë Grace Moretz and Oscar nominee Saoirse
Ronan, so when Disney announced the casting

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:36.340
of a young British actress named Daisy Ridley,
Hollywood let out a collective exclamation

00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:37.520
of "Who?"

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:42.440
Prior to her Star Wars audition, Ridley had
limited exposure to an international audience,

00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:47.370
appearing mostly in British films and television,
but her audition for The Force Awakens changed

00:00:47.370 --> 00:00:48.370
everything.

00:00:48.370 --> 00:00:52.580
For her screen test, Ridley had to perform
a scene in which her character is tortured

00:00:52.580 --> 00:00:54.470
by the film's villain, Kylo Ren.

00:00:54.470 --> 00:00:57.829
"When we brought her in, I asked her to do
this one scene, sort of this one torture scene,

00:00:57.829 --> 00:00:59.180
very sort of intense.

00:00:59.180 --> 00:01:00.730
And she just blew my mind.

00:01:00.730 --> 00:01:04.670
She's reaching this depth of struggle, and
tears are streaming down her face.

00:01:04.670 --> 00:01:05.850
I thought, this is unbelievable."

00:01:05.850 --> 00:01:10.470
Director J.J. Abrams and producer Kathleen
Kennedy were impressed, and Ridley became

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:14.920
one of the first actors cast in the film,
which unsurprisingly went on to become the

00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:19.510
highest-grossing movie of 2015, thanks, of
course, to The Force.

00:01:19.510 --> 00:01:22.240
"That's not how the Force works!"

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:23.900
(Chewbacca sound)

00:01:23.900 --> 00:01:25.180
Hugh Jackman

00:01:25.180 --> 00:01:30.250
The original X-Men in 2000 introduced the
world to Hugh Jackman, and the actor has relished

00:01:30.250 --> 00:01:32.390
his A-list status ever since.

00:01:32.390 --> 00:01:36.730
Prior to playing Wolverine, Jackman had mostly
worked on the Australian stage, performing

00:01:36.730 --> 00:01:39.840
in musicals like Oklahoma! and Sunset Boulevard.

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:43.961
That all changed when a casting director eyed
him to play the hairy, clawed mutant, though

00:01:43.961 --> 00:01:47.070
his initial audition was very low-key for
the berserker.

00:01:47.070 --> 00:01:49.580
"I'm not like you."

00:01:49.580 --> 00:01:52.770
"Oh right, you're just a normal, everyday
claw-guy."

00:01:52.770 --> 00:01:55.950
"Listen kid, about the only thing you've done
to endear yourself to me is to get me into

00:01:55.950 --> 00:01:56.770
a fight, so listen to me.

00:01:56.770 --> 00:01:57.760
Shut up."

00:01:57.940 --> 00:02:02.800
Director Bryan Singer loved Jackman's audition,
but Fox studio executives weren't convinced,

00:02:02.810 --> 00:02:06.600
and wanted a bigger name, initially casting
Dougray Scott in the part.

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:11.049
When Scott had to decline the role due to
scheduling conflicts, Singer turned back to

00:02:11.049 --> 00:02:14.470
Jackman, giving him a screen test opposite
actress Anna Paquin.

00:02:14.470 --> 00:02:18.349
This time, he won the role, despite his wife's
objections.

00:02:18.349 --> 00:02:23.230
"I like to say it was my business plan, it
was a complete fluke.

00:02:23.230 --> 00:02:24.290
Deb said 'you shouldn't do it.'

00:02:24.290 --> 00:02:28.279
She thought it was a terrible idea to do Wolverine.

00:02:28.279 --> 00:02:29.859
The only time in 20 years she's been wrong.

00:02:29.859 --> 00:02:32.129
Please and you feel free to edit that out."

00:02:32.129 --> 00:02:33.159
Harrison Ford

00:02:33.159 --> 00:02:38.090
It's hard to imagine now, but Harrison Ford
had a difficult time in Hollywood after relocating

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:40.269
from his native state of Wisconsin.

00:02:40.269 --> 00:02:45.419
He initially managed to secure small TV roles
and a few bit parts in films, but for ten

00:02:45.419 --> 00:02:50.279
years, he continued to struggle financially,
supplementing his income by working as a stagehand

00:02:50.279 --> 00:02:51.279
and carpenter.

00:02:51.279 --> 00:02:55.620
That's where Ford caught the attention of
casting director Fred Roos, who recommended

00:02:55.620 --> 00:02:59.109
him for American Graffiti, directed by George
Lucas.

00:02:59.109 --> 00:03:02.769
Despite the film's success, Ford still struggled
to find roles.

00:03:02.769 --> 00:03:07.010
Years later, an actor scheduled to read for
the role of Star Wars' resident space scoundrel

00:03:07.010 --> 00:03:10.590
Han Solo failed to show up for his read.

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:11.750
"Scoundrel?

00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:12.900
Scoundrel?

00:03:15.660 --> 00:03:17.299
I like the sound of that."

00:03:17.299 --> 00:03:22.019
George Lucas contacted Ford to come in while
actresses tested for the female lead.

00:03:22.019 --> 00:03:26.099
The director saw something special in Ford
and asked him for his own audition.

00:03:26.099 --> 00:03:29.400
"Well I'm not gonna take you on an impossible
chase across the galaxy.

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:31.809
I was paid to bring you here and now you're
here.

00:03:31.809 --> 00:03:34.400
Give me my other five thousand and I'll be
on my way.

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:35.400
You're on you're own.

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:36.400
I'm on my own.

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:38.019
I'll let you off on the nearest system."

00:03:38.019 --> 00:03:40.389
Also reading for the role of Han Solo?

00:03:40.389 --> 00:03:42.139
A young Kurt Russell.

00:03:42.139 --> 00:03:43.180
Sigourney Weaver

00:03:43.180 --> 00:03:46.889
Though it would be years before she impressed
audiences with her vocal abilities…

00:03:46.889 --> 00:03:50.469
"There is no Dana only Zuul."

00:03:50.469 --> 00:03:53.879
"What a lovely singing voice you must have."

00:03:53.879 --> 00:03:59.650
...Sigourney Weaver began her career off-Broadway,
having graduated from Yale's drama program.

00:03:59.650 --> 00:04:05.309
After kind of appearing in a small, very small
role in Woody Allen's hit Annie Hall, a casting

00:04:05.309 --> 00:04:09.919
director suggested Weaver to director Ridley
Scott, who was casting a new science fiction

00:04:09.919 --> 00:04:11.099
film called Alien.

00:04:11.099 --> 00:04:14.959
"Oh I'll get off your back, as soon as 12
module is fixed."

00:04:14.959 --> 00:04:16.410
"We're working on it.

00:04:16.410 --> 00:04:18.220
I only got two hands."

00:04:18.220 --> 00:04:22.350
"Well put down your beer can and use both
of them and maybe you'll get it done."

00:04:22.350 --> 00:04:27.260
Scott had trouble deciding between Weaver
and a friend and co-star of hers, Meryl Streep,

00:04:27.260 --> 00:04:29.070
since both had tested for the part.

00:04:29.070 --> 00:04:33.230
He invited several women from the production
office to view the two screen tests, and the

00:04:33.230 --> 00:04:36.010
women immediately said Weaver as their favorite.

00:04:36.010 --> 00:04:41.100
Alien would become an international sensation,
spawning a number of sequels and making Weaver

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:42.100
a star.

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:47.090
Three Oscar nominations later, it's safe to
say Scott made a good choice with Weaver.

00:04:47.090 --> 00:04:48.430
Christopher Reeve

00:04:48.430 --> 00:04:53.470
He's the most popular superhero in the world,
so casting Superman in his first, big, full-color

00:04:53.470 --> 00:04:58.440
theatrical outing was a pretty big deal for
producers Ilya and Alexander Salkind.

00:04:58.440 --> 00:05:02.660
After hiring director Richard Donner to helm
the production, the creative team auditioned

00:05:02.660 --> 00:05:07.570
established stars like James Caan and Paul
Newman, and even then-unknown bodybuilder

00:05:07.570 --> 00:05:09.230
Arnold Schwarzenegger.

00:05:09.230 --> 00:05:13.410
Casting director Lynn Stalmaster suggested
a young actor named Christopher Reeve, who'd

00:05:13.410 --> 00:05:18.690
studied drama at the esteemed Juilliard school
and had a number of stage credits to his name.

00:05:18.690 --> 00:05:23.200
Donner and the Salkinds first resisted casting
Reeve, deeming him too thin.

00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:27.470
Still, at the insistence of Stalmaster, Donner
allowed Reeve to do a screen test.

00:05:27.470 --> 00:05:29.910
"Oh I come from a planet in the Xeno galaxy.

00:05:29.910 --> 00:05:31.090
A place called Krypton.

00:05:31.090 --> 00:05:32.080
"Krypton?

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:33.140
With a C-R-Y?"

00:05:33.520 --> 00:05:34.520
"No.

00:05:34.800 --> 00:05:36.800
No, actually it's Krypton, with a K-R-Y."

00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:41.310
The director would later recall that when
he saw Reeve, dressed in the full Superman

00:05:41.310 --> 00:05:45.590
costume, jump onto the screen for the first
time, he knew he'd found his Superman.

00:05:45.590 --> 00:05:50.110
Reeve would go on to play the role in three
subsequent sequels, becoming a cultural icon

00:05:50.110 --> 00:05:51.340
along the way.

00:05:51.340 --> 00:05:52.340
Gabourey Sidibe

00:05:52.340 --> 00:05:58.530
The 1996 novel Push had become something of
a cult sensation by 2009 when film director

00:05:58.530 --> 00:06:01.520
Lee Daniels selected it as his next film project.

00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:07.110
The story about an abused teenage girl attracted
acclaim as well as criticism for its raw,

00:06:07.110 --> 00:06:08.550
dark themes.

00:06:08.550 --> 00:06:12.330
Casting the right person in the lead role
was vital, as most of the drama of the story

00:06:12.330 --> 00:06:14.900
would fall on the shoulders of the leading
actress.

00:06:14.900 --> 00:06:20.000
The film, which was retitled Precious, offered
an open call for actresses to audition regardless

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:21.090
of experience.

00:06:21.090 --> 00:06:25.930
Gabourey Sidibe heard about the audition,
but she'd never acted on screen before.

00:06:25.930 --> 00:06:30.530
Fortunately, Sidibe gave a stunning audition,
beating out 300 other girls.

00:06:30.530 --> 00:06:31.030
"For what?

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:33.380
How?

00:06:34.850 --> 00:06:41.690
I feel like, like I'm drowning in a giant
river."

00:06:41.690 --> 00:06:46.090
Sidibe filmed the movie in only a few weeks,
but Precious would go on to become a lasting

00:06:46.090 --> 00:06:52.380
critical and commercial sensation, earning
her a Best Actress Academy Award nomination.

00:06:52.380 --> 00:06:53.380
Daniel Radcliffe

00:06:53.380 --> 00:06:57.730
The Harry Potter book series was already a
pop culture phenomenon by the time Warner

00:06:57.730 --> 00:07:03.000
Bros. won the rights to produce film adaptations
of the series' first four books in 1998.

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:07.111
The series would face one main logistical
problem: with each book set a year apart,

00:07:07.111 --> 00:07:11.620
all of the films would need to be filmed in
rapid succession so that their child actors

00:07:11.620 --> 00:07:13.000
would age naturally.

00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:17.590
An 11-year-old actor named Daniel Radcliffe
attracted the attention of producer David

00:07:17.590 --> 00:07:18.590
Heyman.

00:07:18.590 --> 00:07:22.440
Radcliffe had acted in a just a couple of
British television productions before scoring

00:07:22.440 --> 00:07:26.920
his audition for Harry Potter, and had to
audition several times over a period of eight

00:07:26.920 --> 00:07:29.220
months before his final screen test.

00:07:29.220 --> 00:07:30.120
"That's a dragon egg.

00:07:30.220 --> 00:07:31.220
That's what that is

00:07:31.580 --> 00:07:32.580
But what did you get it, Hagrid?

00:07:32.700 --> 00:07:34.220
It must've cost you a fortune."

00:07:34.610 --> 00:07:35.610
J.K.

00:07:35.610 --> 00:07:40.420
Rowling gave her approval, and just like that,
Radcliffe was the face of a blockbuster franchise.

00:07:40.420 --> 00:07:42.820
And then...he'd go on to play a farting corpse.

00:07:47.540 --> 00:07:49.220
No points for Gryffindor on that one.

00:07:49.900 --> 00:07:50.800
Thanks for watching!

00:07:50.800 --> 00:07:53.770
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:07:53.770 --> 00:07:56.530
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

